{"type":"assistant","uuid":"7358062f-31c3-48c4-b826-6b8b44670318","session_id":"e327d0e3-73e7-4f4c-8b87-2f74b17b1c30","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"7358062f-31c3-48c4-b826-6b8b44670318","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The exploration agent is still running. Let me proceed with the fix since I've already gathered enough information from reading the source code. The bug is clear:\n\nIn `ManageFishingSpotFragment.verifyUserInput()`, coordinates are read from the map's camera position instead of from the TextView inputs. The fix is to read from the TextViews.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"3f6b0ac4-0fb6-4c84-bee7-baf4b4a2d636","session_id":"e327d0e3-73e7-4f4c-8b87-2f74b17b1c30","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"3f6b0ac4-0fb6-4c84-bee7-baf4b4a2d636","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my thorough analysis, I've identified the root cause of the bug. Here's the issue:\n\n**Root Cause:** In `ManageFishingSpotFragment.verifyUserInput()`, coordinates are always read from the map's camera position (`mMap.getCameraPosition().target.latitude`), NOT from the manually entered TextView inputs. When a user types coordinates directly into the latitude/longitude fields and saves without clicking the sync button, the map's camera position is stale/wrong, so the saved coordinates are incorrect.\n\n**Fix:** Read coordinates from the `mLatitudeView` and `mLongitudeView` TextViews in `verifyUserInput()`, using the existing `validateCoordinateInput()` helper method.\n\nLet me implement the fix:\n\n"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
