{"type":"assistant","uuid":"2662161d-1c5f-470c-afd3-f59216b094b1","session_id":"e327d0e3-73e7-4f4c-8b87-2f74b17b1c30","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"2662161d-1c5f-470c-afd3-f59216b094b1","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build succeeds. Here's a summary of the fix:\n\n## Bug Analysis\n\n**File:** `app/src/main/java/com/cohenadair/anglerslog/locations/ManageFishingSpotFragment.java`\n\n**Root Cause:** In the `verifyUserInput()` method, coordinates were always read from the map's camera position (`mMap.getCameraPosition().target.latitude/longitude`), completely ignoring the values the user manually typed into the latitude/longitude `InputTextView` widgets. The \"sync\" (refresh) button was the only mechanism that updated the map from TextView input — but if the user skipped it and saved directly, the stale map position was used instead.\n\n**Flow before fix:**\n1. User manually enters coordinates in TextView → map position unchanged\n2. User clicks Save → `verifyUserInput()` reads from **map camera position** (stale) → wrong coordinates saved\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nChanged `verifyUserInput()` to read coordinates from the `mLatitudeView` and `mLongitudeView` TextViews first using the existing `validateCoordinateInput()` helper. Only if the TextViews are empty/invalid does it fall back to the map camera position or default values.\n\n**Flow after fix:**\n1. User manually enters coordinates in TextView → map position may be unchanged (cosmetic only)\n2. User clicks Save → `verifyUserInput()` reads from **TextView inputs** → correct coordinates saved\n3. If TextViews are empty/invalid → falls back to map camera position (preserving existing behavior for map-only input)"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42427,"output_tokens":345,"cache_read_input_tokens":40128,"total_tokens":42772}}}
